## The Solitaire Sweet Spot

The Solitaire Sweet Spot is the 1.5ct mark for a custom radiant pendant. At 1ct, a radiant diamond pendant reads as fine jewelry — elegant but subtle. At 2ct and above, it becomes a statement piece that draws attention — and the 1.5ct sits exactly between those two positions.

At 1.5ct, a radiant cut measures approximately 8.0×6.1mm for an elongated stone. That face-up size sits at the centre of the decolletage in a way that is immediately visible but not overwhelming — which is why most buyers who want a radiant pendant for daily wear land between 1ct and 1.5ct. On a delicate chain at 16–18 inches, a 1.5ct radiant reads from a normal conversational distance without needing direct lighting.

The price difference between a 1ct and 1.5ct natural radiant stone is significant — a [1ct G-VS2 GIA stone starts at $2,318](https://www.bluenile.com/diamond-details/25995245?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational), while a [1.5ct G-VS2 GIA stone starts at $7,704](https://www.bluenile.com/diamond-details/29651855?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational), more than three times the price for half a carat more. In lab, the jump is smaller: a [1ct E-VVS1 IGI stone at $867](https://www.bluenile.com/diamond-details/29417414?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational) versus a [1.5ct F-VVS1 IGI stone at $1,510](https://www.bluenile.com/diamond-details/29569681?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational).

For buyers who want the visible presence without reaching 2ct weight, the 1.5ct natural or 1.5ct lab stone is where most decisions land. It is the target for everyday-wear radiant pendant buyers.

