## Design Your Own: Natural Radiant Cut Pendant Prices

The [design-your-own pendant tool](https://www.bluenile.com/diamond-jewelry/diamond-necklaces/design-your-own-diamond-pendant?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational) lets you choose a specific GIA-certified radiant cut loose stone and pair it with a pendant setting of your choice. The prices below are stone-only from certified market inventory. Add a pendant setting — typically $150–400 for a simple prong or bezel style in the tool — to get your complete pendant price.

At 1ct, natural radiant cut stones span a meaningful quality range. A [G-VS2 GIA stone at $2,318](https://www.bluenile.com/diamond-details/25995245?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational) is a clean, near-colorless stone — appropriate for any pendant setting. At the premium end, a [D-VVS2 GIA stone at $3,594](https://www.bluenile.com/diamond-details/29587972?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational) is a colorless, near-flawless stone at roughly 1.5× the entry price.

At 1.5ct, the price jump is real. The natural 1.5ct entry at [$7,704](https://www.bluenile.com/diamond-details/29651855?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational) for a G-VS2 GIA stone reflects that radiant cut natural diamonds scale steeply at the 1.5ct mark. The face-up size is approximately 8.0×6.1mm — visibly larger on the neckline at any conversational distance.

At 2ct natural, you are in a different market. The entry point is [$17,714](https://www.bluenile.com/diamond-details/16750163?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational) for a D-VS2 GIA stone — a 2ct natural radiant pendant is a statement piece, not an everyday accessory.

