| [2ct G-VVS1 Radiant](https://www.bluenile.com/diamond-details/23974327?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational) | GIA | [$21,044](https://www.bluenile.com/diamond-details/23974327?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational) | + [setting](https://www.bluenile.com/diamond-jewelry/diamond-necklaces/design-your-own-diamond-pendant?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational) | G color at VVS1 clarity — near-flawless certificate at 2ct. [$3,330](https://www.bluenile.com/diamond-details/23974327?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational) more than the D-VS2 entry for a lower color, higher clarity. Only makes sense when the VVS1 grade is personally meaningful. |

**Verdict:** For most natural pendant buyers, the [1.5ct E-VS1 GIA at $7,844](https://www.bluenile.com/diamond-details/28090460?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational) is the strongest pick in this table. E color at VS1 clarity is a clean stone with an excellent certificate for a daily-wear pendant — and it arrives almost identically priced to the G-VS2 entry at only [$140](https://www.bluenile.com/diamond-details/28090460?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational) more. At 1ct, the [F-VS1 at $2,787](https://www.bluenile.com/diamond-details/29538475?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational) is the quality sweet spot.

