## Design Your Own: Lab Radiant Cut Pendant Prices

Lab radiant cut diamonds are IGI-certified and chemically identical to natural diamonds. They are not subject to the natural scarcity premium — which is why a [1ct lab radiant stone starts at $867](https://www.bluenile.com/diamond-details/29417414?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational) versus $2,318 for the natural entry at the same carat.

At 1ct lab, you can access D-grade stones with VVS1 clarity for under $1,000. At 1.5ct lab, the [$1,510 F-VVS1 IGI stone](https://www.bluenile.com/diamond-details/29569681?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational) gives you [The Solitaire Sweet Spot](#the-solitaire-sweet-spot) face-up size at roughly one-fifth the cost of the natural equivalent. At 2ct lab, the [F-VVS1 IGI stone at $2,169](https://www.bluenile.com/diamond-details/27801066?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational) opens up carat sizes that most natural budgets cannot reach for a daily-wear piece.

For lab pendants, add a pendant setting from the [design-your-own tool](https://www.bluenile.com/diamond-jewelry/diamond-necklaces/design-your-own-diamond-pendant?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational) — typically $150–400 for a standard prong or bezel style — to your stone price to get the complete pendant total.

| Stone | Cert | Stone Price | Pendant Setting | What this means |
|-------|------|-------------|-----------------|-----------------|
| [1ct E-VVS1 Radiant Lab](https://www.bluenile.com/diamond-details/29417414?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational) | IGI | [$867](https://www.bluenile.com/diamond-details/29417414?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational) | + [setting](https://www.bluenile.com/diamond-jewelry/diamond-necklaces/design-your-own-diamond-pendant?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational) | **Lab entry.** E-VVS1 IGI at 1ct. The lowest price for a certified lab radiant solitaire pendant. For buyers who want maximum value at the smallest budget — excellent stone, excellent certificate. |
| [1ct D-VVS1 Radiant Lab](https://www.bluenile.com/diamond-details/24946874?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational) | IGI | [$932](https://www.bluenile.com/diamond-details/24946874?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational) | + [setting](https://www.bluenile.com/diamond-jewelry/diamond-necklaces/design-your-own-diamond-pendant?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational) | D color at VVS1 — the top grade combination at 1ct lab for [$65](https://www.bluenile.com/diamond-details/24946874?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational) more than the E-VVS1. At pendant-on-neckline distance, D and E are indistinguishable. The [$65](https://www.bluenile.com/diamond-details/24946874?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational) is worth it when the certificate grade matters. |
