| [2ct E-VVS1 Radiant Lab](https://www.bluenile.com/diamond-details/26351307?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational) | IGI | [$2,220](https://www.bluenile.com/diamond-details/26351307?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational) | + [setting](https://www.bluenile.com/diamond-jewelry/diamond-necklaces/design-your-own-diamond-pendant?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational) | E-VVS1 at 2ct lab — [$51](https://www.bluenile.com/diamond-details/26351307?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational) more than the F-VVS1 for one color grade. Both are correct choices. |

**Verdict:** The [1.5ct F-VVS1 IGI at $1,510](https://www.bluenile.com/diamond-details/29569681?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational) is the best value in the lab pendant table — the same face-up size as the [$7,844 natural equivalent](https://www.bluenile.com/diamond-details/28090460?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational), for a stone price more than five times lower. At 1ct, the [D-VVS1 IGI at $932](https://www.bluenile.com/diamond-details/24946874?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational) gives you the best-grade certificate for under $1,000.

> **Farzana on Lab vs Natural Pendants:**
>
> At pendant-on-neckline distance, no one can tell the difference between a lab radiant and a natural radiant. Both have the same face-up size, the same crushed-ice sparkle, the same shape. The only things that differ are the certificate origin and the price tag.
>
> For a daily-wear piece, lab makes the most practical sense. You are not insuring a [$7,844](https://www.bluenile.com/diamond-details/28090460?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational) stone worn every day — you are insuring a [$1,510](https://www.bluenile.com/diamond-details/29569681?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational) stone. That practical difference is worth considering before you choose.

## The Eternity Tier

The Eternity Tier is what the [36.75ct lab radiant diamond eternity necklace at $32,929](https://www.bluenile.com/jewelry/necklaces/lab-grown-radiant-diamond-eternity-necklace-in-18k-yellow-gold-36-1-2-ct-tw-item-282745?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational) represents: a complete collar of individually-set radiant diamonds where the necklace itself is the statement, not a single pendant.

This necklace has 102 prong-set radiant cut lab diamonds across a 17-inch chain in 18K yellow gold, with F-G average color and VS1-VS2 average clarity. The total carat weight is 36.75ct — each stone averaging approximately 0.36ct at 5.1mm — creating a seamless wall of crushed-ice sparkle across the full neckline.

At [$32,929](https://www.bluenile.com/jewelry/necklaces/lab-grown-radiant-diamond-eternity-necklace-in-18k-yellow-gold-36-1-2-ct-tw-item-282745?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational), this is not an everyday purchase — it is a high-fine-jewelry decision. The price reflects the 102-stone count, the 18K yellow gold, and the total carat weight rather than the per-stone value. Lab pricing makes this achievable at a fraction of the natural equivalent — a comparable natural version would price into seven figures.

The eternity necklace wears differently from a pendant. A pendant sits at the decolletage as a single point of light. The eternity necklace creates a full horizontal band of radiant sparkle across the collarbone — for black-tie events, formal dinners, or daily wear that invites attention, it is unmatched in this shape.

