## Frequently Asked Questions

### How much does a radiant cut diamond necklace cost?

A radiant cut diamond necklace starts at [$867](https://www.bluenile.com/diamond-details/29417414?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational) for a lab-grown 1ct E-VVS1 IGI stone (plus a pendant setting via the [design-your-own tool](https://www.bluenile.com/diamond-jewelry/diamond-necklaces/design-your-own-diamond-pendant?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational)), [$2,318](https://www.bluenile.com/diamond-details/25995245?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational) for a natural 1ct G-VS2 GIA stone, and [$32,929](https://www.bluenile.com/jewelry/necklaces/lab-grown-radiant-diamond-eternity-necklace-in-18k-yellow-gold-36-1-2-ct-tw-item-282745?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational) for the pre-made 36.75ct lab radiant eternity necklace. Custom natural 1.5ct pendants start around [$7,704](https://www.bluenile.com/diamond-details/29651855?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational) for the stone before adding a setting.

### What is a radiant cut diamond pendant?

A radiant cut diamond pendant is a necklace featuring a single radiant cut diamond — a rectangular or square stone with a hybrid brilliant and step-cut facet pattern — set in a prong, bezel, or halo pendant setting and hung on a chain. The radiant cut's crushed-ice facets scatter light in multiple directions, which makes the pendant sparkle during movement rather than only under direct light.

### Is lab or natural better for a radiant cut diamond necklace?

For daily wear, lab is the more practical choice. A [1.5ct lab F-VVS1 IGI stone at $1,510](https://www.bluenile.com/diamond-details/29569681?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational) delivers the same face-up size as a [$7,844 natural equivalent](https://www.bluenile.com/diamond-details/28090460?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational) at one-fifth the cost. At necklace distance, lab and natural are visually indistinguishable — natural makes sense when origin and resale value matter or when the GIA certificate is a personal priority.

### What carat size is best for a radiant cut diamond pendant?

1.5ct is [The Solitaire Sweet Spot](#the-solitaire-sweet-spot) for a radiant pendant — at approximately 8.0×6.1mm, it is clearly visible at conversational distance and light enough for daily wear. 1ct is the subtle choice for buyers who want elegance without calling attention. 2ct crosses into statement-pendant territory — best for formal occasions or dedicated wearers. The 36.75ct eternity necklace is its own category.

### What chain length is best for a radiant cut diamond pendant?

An 18-inch chain is the most versatile — it sits just below the collarbone and works with most necklines. For V-necks or lower cuts, a 20-inch chain positions the stone in the decolletage deliberately. For maximum visibility, a 16-inch chain keeps the stone near the collarbone where it is visible with any neckline, including crew necks and higher cuts.

### What is the radiant cut diamond eternity necklace price?

The [lab radiant diamond eternity necklace in 18K yellow gold (item 282745)](https://www.bluenile.com/jewelry/necklaces/lab-grown-radiant-diamond-eternity-necklace-in-18k-yellow-gold-36-1-2-ct-tw-item-282745?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational) is [$32,929](https://www.bluenile.com/jewelry/necklaces/lab-grown-radiant-diamond-eternity-necklace-in-18k-yellow-gold-36-1-2-ct-tw-item-282745?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational) with 36.75ct total weight, 102 individually prong-set lab radiant diamonds, F-G average color, VS1-VS2 average clarity, on a 17-inch chain. A natural equivalent at comparable weight and quality would price into seven figures.

### What color is best for a radiant cut diamond pendant?

F color in white gold or platinum is the sweet spot for a radiant pendant — delivers a colorless appearance at necklace distance without the D or E price premium. In lab, D-VVS1 is available at [$932](https://www.bluenile.com/diamond-details/24946874?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational) at 1ct — always take the D in lab when the price premium is minimal. G is acceptable in white gold; H+ is better in yellow or rose gold settings.

### What clarity is best for a radiant cut diamond pendant?

VS1 is the recommended minimum clarity for a radiant pendant — at necklace distance, inclusions at VS1 are invisible without magnification. In lab, VVS1 often costs the same as VS1 — take it. VS2 at 1.5ct or above needs eye-clean confirmation in a 10× video before buying, and SI1 is not recommended for a radiant pendant at any price.

### Can I design my own radiant cut diamond pendant?

Yes — Blue Nile's [design-your-own diamond pendant tool](https://www.bluenile.com/diamond-jewelry/diamond-necklaces/design-your-own-diamond-pendant?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational) lets you choose a specific GIA or IGI-certified radiant loose stone and pair it with a setting of your choice. Select the stone ID you want from the certified inventory, choose your setting style and metal, and configure your chain length. The custom route gives you full control over the specific stone going into your pendant.

### What is a radiant cut diamond pendant vs radiant cut pendant necklace?

These terms describe the same thing — a necklace featuring a radiant cut diamond stone as the main pendant. "Radiant cut pendant" and "radiant cut pendant necklace" both refer to a solitaire-style necklace where a single radiant diamond is set in a pendant and hung on a chain. The distinction is from "radiant cut diamond necklace" which also covers eternity or tennis-style necklaces with multiple radiant stones, like the [36.75ct eternity at $32,929](https://www.bluenile.com/jewelry/necklaces/lab-grown-radiant-diamond-eternity-necklace-in-18k-yellow-gold-36-1-2-ct-tw-item-282745?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational).

### What is the difference between a radiant cut and emerald cut diamond pendant?

Both are rectangular step-adjacent cuts, but they behave differently in a pendant. A radiant cut has a brilliant-hybrid facet pattern — the crushed-ice sparkle scatters light in multiple directions and is especially visible during movement. An emerald cut is a true step cut that shows long hall-of-mirrors flashes most visible when the stone is still — radiant pendants attract attention during movement, emerald pendants under direct light.

### How do I care for a radiant cut diamond pendant necklace?

Clean your radiant pendant with warm water, a small amount of mild soap, and a soft brush — the prongs and setting corners collect oils from daily wear. A radiant cut's corners are slightly trimmed by the facets but can still collect debris. Remove the pendant during high-impact activities, swimming, and sleeping — and store the [eternity necklace](https://www.bluenile.com/jewelry/necklaces/lab-grown-radiant-diamond-eternity-necklace-in-18k-yellow-gold-36-1-2-ct-tw-item-282745?a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational) flat rather than coiled to avoid stressing the individual stone settings.

